1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,380
All right, first years, come introduce yourselves.

2
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:07,320
Yes, sir!

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:13,140
Hi, my name is Koshi Sugawara, and I'm a setter, and I come from Nagamushi.

4
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,100
It is a pleasure to meet you.

5
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:21,300
I... I'm Asi Azumane, and I play left-sided Sekodai.

6
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:22,740
I'm a pleasure to meet you, too.

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,820
Oh, crap.

8
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,460
My name is Daiichi Sawamura. I'm from Azumadate.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,540
I play left, too. I saw Karasuno play at Nationals.

10
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:37,540
That's why I chose this school. Looking forward to playing with you.

11
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:41,240
Oh, yeah? Well, there you go. I like your enthusiasm.

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,020
Then why don't we aim for Nationals this year?

13
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:44,960
Yes, sir!

14
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:49,580
I'm Tashiro, the team captain, and I cannot wait to work with you guys.

15
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:52,140
You kids have fun now. I'll drop by later.

16
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:55,280
See ya. All right, let's get to practicing.

17
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:56,080
Okay!

18
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:00,900
So I guess the guy who just walked out is our advisor?

19
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:03,420
Is there, like, a coach on the way or something?

20
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:05,800
There's no coach.

21
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:11,040
Wait, wasn't that Kurokawa from Issa Middle School?

22
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,180
So you know him?

23
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:15,600
I played against him. His attacks were so incredible.

24
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:16,660
Defense, too.

25
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:17,660
Oh!

26
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,380
Really? That's so cool!

27
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:23,140
We're finally here at the famous Karasuno!

28
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:23,800
Boy, you know.

29
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:32,560
Okay.

30
00:01:32,560 --> 00:02:02,540
Thank you.

31
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:32,540
Thank you.

32
00:02:32,560 --> 00:03:02,540
Thank you.

33
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,060
Aw.

34
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:08,280
Hey, Kurokawa, could you maybe give me some pointers on my receives?

35
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:12,260
The moment I see the opponent hit the ball, I just get ready for it.

36
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:13,580
Uh, okay.

37
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:18,600
Time to wrap up!

38
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,900
Yes, sir!

39
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:24,460
Hey, the tournament is coming up. Shouldn't we have some practice matches?

40
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:30,320
They said that ever since Coach Yukai left, our relationships with other schools have been slowly falling apart.

41
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:36,760
Yeah, I heard there was a school they were practicing with right before we got here. And now even those guys have turned us down.

42
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,120
Huh? Why's that?

43
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,500
They don't see the point wasting any of their time working with us.

44
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:47,040
I knew Kurasuna wasn't the team it used to be.

45
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:53,360
But I thought if we practiced hard enough, we could bring it back to its former greatness.

46
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:59,280
It didn't feel like a hopeless situation, nor was there any huge conflict.

47
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:08,960
However, there was still a lingering fear that we were losing our way.

48
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:24,520
Um, so, would you guys mind if I practiced a little more? I'll lock up afterwards.

49
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,480
Uh, me too, if that's cool.

50
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,240
Me three! I'll go tell the advisor.

51
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,580
Uh, sure.

52
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:36,880
We can't go on like this. Nationals aren't far away.

53
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:38,300
Oh, you sound like a teacher.

54
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:41,600
Yeah, or a dad. Are you sure you're just a first year?

55
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,560
If we keep learning, then we'll keep getting better.

56
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,080
Yeah!

57
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,740
The Spiker's form shows the ball's corpse.

58
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,260
Hey, you're not supposed to catch it.

59
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,420
I'm sorry!

60
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:07,340
We'll find ways to learn and grow.

61
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:13,600
We just have to keep our chins up and work hard at improving.

62
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:17,480
Tomorrow's the qualifying tournament for Nationals.

63
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,640
You only get one shot, boys.

64
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:20,660
Yes, sir!

65
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,740
Winning Nationals is our only goal!

66
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:31,880
Dude, I've been thinking, maybe we should be setting our goals as something that we actually have a chance of achieving.

67
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:32,340
Huh?

68
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:37,840
You can lose a lot of your self-confidence if you try setting the bar too high, and nobody wants that, right?

69
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,940
Whoa! You okay, man?

70
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:45,780
Up until now, you've always given me a dirty look or just ignored me whenever I said we were going to Nationals.

71
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:46,660
But not now.

72
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,760
Now you're finally biting back!

73
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,700
I love it!

74
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:52,240
You have any idea why that makes me so happy?

75
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,240
Uh, not really.

76
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:59,960
Maybe we aren't on the same page as far as goals go, but we've come a long way and we get along really well now.

77
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:03,780
Plus, we all have this burning desire to win the next game, right, guys?

78
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,180
So let's go win!

79
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:06,140
Yeah!

80
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:08,780
Ha-ha!

81
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:12,500
And then, the Miyagi Prefecture Prelims.

82
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,560
We lost in the second round.

83
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:21,500
And our third years retired from club activities.

84
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:26,600
I guess that means our crows have fallen.

85
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:37,360
Damn, maybe we realized the value of teamwork too late.

86
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:39,680
It's true.

87
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,820
Chance really does favor the prepared.

88
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,460
That's where we screwed up.

89
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,900
I feel like we've hit rock bottom.

90
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,180
Karasuno might never come back from this slump.

91
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:52,220
Or if we do, it might be in the distant future.

92
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,360
Who knows?

93
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:58,020
Even so, if you get another chance, then take it!

94
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:06,920
Now, now is our chance, and we're gonna take it!

95
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:15,900
They haven't been guarding against Hinata's blocks until recently, so I can tell it's getting under their skin.

96
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:23,500
Even if it's only a small crack in their armor, it'll prove to be useful for us in the end.

97
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,900
It's a chance, Ball!

98
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:28,780
Damn it!

99
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,120
All right, we finally took the lead from them.

100
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,540
Now, don't give it back!

101
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,040
Gatsuki!

102
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:36,160
I'm a second too late!

103
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,680
They're definitely taking notice of Hinata now.

104
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,440
It can't be ignored.

105
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,620
That's gonna be a straight!

106
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:48,700
Leave this to me!

107
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:56,700
Nice kill!

108
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:59,160
We can't let Hinata have all the fun, right?

109
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,260
Hey, Kageyama!

110
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,360
Nice receive!

111
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:01,880
Thanks!

112
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,860
This one's got a strong serve.

113
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,220
Let's nip it in the bud!

114
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:15,940
Yeah!

115
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:21,680
Nishidara!

116
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,100
Sorry, that's long!

117
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,180
Hold your ground, Goshiki.

118
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:30,100
Kurosuno Setter is in the back row, so they aren't gonna dump.

119
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:31,320
Just watch closely.

120
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:33,920
What?

121
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,140
He's already here?

122
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,180
Shit!

123
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:43,420
It's this far into the game, and their moves are still so sharp.

124
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:45,540
These guys are machines!

125
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:51,340
It doesn't matter how many times they've practiced it before, that move is always gonna be tough

126
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:52,060
to pull off.

127
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,100
You're in, Specs!

128
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:55,980
About time!

129
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:57,780
I thought they'd never take number 10 out.

130
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:58,740
Suki!

131
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:01,080
Don't let Hinata beat you!

132
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,260
Huh?

133
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:02,640
Huh?

134
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:06,980
Yeah, like there's any comparison.

135
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:12,620
Kageyama.

136
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:13,000
Yeah?

137
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,300
You got this.

138
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:14,920
Right.

139
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,060
I can do this.

140
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,700
What about you, Tsukishima?

141
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,860
Well, I worked a bit with Akashi.

142
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:26,980
This jerk's been practicing with Vukorodani Setter?

143
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,960
Makes me kinda jealous.

144
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:30,480
Ginger!

145
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:32,340
Come sit down.

146
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:34,280
Take any chance you can to rest.

147
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,460
Conserve your energy.

148
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,040
Okay.

149
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:40,080
I don't wanna lose to Hinata either.

150
00:09:40,860 --> 00:09:43,300
This time, I'm gonna prove myself worthy.

151
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,780
Give us a good serve, Tanashi!

152
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:46,900
Hey, wait.

153
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:49,280
Isn't he a little further back than usual?

154
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:53,580
Your serve could be a valuable weapon.

155
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:55,980
Straight.

156
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,120
Just hit it straight.

157
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:00,200
Toward Ushiwaka.

158
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,180
Yes, we broke through.

159
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:04,620
Keep it up.

160
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:05,020
Go ski!

161
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,120
Got it!

162
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,380
Make him follow.

163
00:10:07,580 --> 00:10:08,600
A three-man block!

164
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,080
Don't underestimate me.

165
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,080
I'll get through!

166
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:15,280
One touch!

167
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,900
Not on my watch now!

168
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:17,600
Nice cover!

169
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,460
A time differential attack?

170
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,720
That's right.

171
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:39,220
You're not the only one who learned some new tricks during training camp.

172
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:39,960
Hinata.

173
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:41,260
Yeah!

174
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:43,640
Whoa!

175
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,280
The rest of them broke through!

176
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:48,000
Damn, that guy in the glasses has some guts.

177
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,320
God damn it!

178
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:51,940
Nice!

179
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:52,680
You can't move!

180
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:54,340
You show off!

181
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,200
You're completely dropping your elbows!

182
00:10:56,540 --> 00:11:00,620
If you lazy nitwits were using proper form, then your spikes would break through everything!

183
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:05,880
You've all got these huge hulking bodies, so you have to be more, uh, more, more, more, more...

184
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:06,540
Dineric!

185
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,300
Yeah!

186
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:16,260
It's true, their defense is good, and they're constantly evolving it, but still, it's just a stopgap measure.

187
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,460
However, there is no such thing as the perfect defense.

188
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:28,320
Unleash the beast, Hanashi!

189
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:28,480
Unleash the beast, Hanashi!

190
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,040
And head next!

191
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:29,560
Front!

192
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,500
On it!

193
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:39,920
I tried to comedy!

194
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,480
At next!

195
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:40,920
Front!

196
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:41,360
On it!

197
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:49,200
Damn it!

198
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,360
Ushiwaka makes it look so easy!

199
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,560
Yeah, but he's hit so many of these by now.

200
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,580
His legs have got to be getting tired.

201
00:11:59,200 --> 00:11:59,500
Uh-huh.

202
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:03,360
If we just hang on, even someone like Ushiwaka will run out of steam.

203
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:10,220
You got this, Asahi!

204
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,760
Got it!

205
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,720
He's off!

206
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,960
Yeah! So gay!

207
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,340
Oh my god, my heart just skipped a beat!

208
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:35,140
Can't believe he pulled that off!

209
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:36,700
We're at set point, right?

210
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,660
It's their first five-set match,

211
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:42,660
and it's against a team that regularly makes it to Nationals.

212
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:47,020
From the fourth set on, this is unexplored territory for our Crows.

213
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:51,680
Since the game started, number nines had to compensate for Shorty's insane attacks.

214
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:55,000
Plus, make sure he gets just the right kind of sets.

215
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:58,200
Precision is also expected out of him.

216
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:01,280
Probably more so than anyone else on that team.

217
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,840
All while being under a lot of pressure to block our advances.

218
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:09,500
Not to mention, he also handles the ball more than any single player.

219
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,780
I'm thinking he'll be the first one to reach his limit.

220
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:14,800
That's my fault!

221
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:16,600
You creep me out when you apologize.

222
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:17,860
I don't accept it.

223
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:18,420
What?

224
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,760
Much better.

225
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:25,160
Daichi, serve us something sweet!

226
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:26,680
The front!

227
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:28,760
Ushiwaka!

228
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:34,760
Damn it!

229
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:43,000
Hey, wait, do you think Shira Torizawa has a second bench server?

230
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,480
It wouldn't surprise me.

231
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:46,300
I'm sure their bench has just about everything.

232
00:13:46,940 --> 00:13:48,080
Hang in there, you guys.

233
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,840
Please don't bring this into a deuce.

234
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,280
Let's do this!

235
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,660
A jump float, serve?

236
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:00,220
Sorry!

237
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:05,480
They picked it up!

238
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:06,440
There's Ushiwaka!

239
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:08,500
Ushiwaka!

240
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,580
On my call, and now!

241
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:17,540
No way!

242
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:22,200
When you're defending one part of the court,

243
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,680
another area will always be vulnerable.

244
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,800
If they're gathered in the back,

245
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,860
then naturally,

246
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:30,340
it leaves the front

247
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,060
wide open.

248
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:42,760
They totally saw it.

249
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:44,500
We left a huge space open.

250
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,220
Yeah, that's true, but still,

251
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,520
I thought Kageyama would have been able to pick that up.

252
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,780
His fatigue must be getting to him.

253
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:53,380
Oh, is the tired Widow Shatter

254
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:55,460
going to have to deal a deuce of despair?

255
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:59,360
Nothing you could do

256
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,060
would bring me despair.

257
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,260
It would only be

258
00:15:03,260 --> 00:15:05,020
if I wasn't able to play volleyball.

259
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,460
You're all just a bunch of

260
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:10,680
jerky

261
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,140
jerkheads.

262
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:29,420
Come on!

263
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,520
Let's go!

264
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:31,540
Let's go!

265
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:33,260
Our defense is fine as is.

266
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,940
Great job on those one touches.

267
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:35,660
Right!

268
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:37,960
Kageyama, you good?

269
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,640
Yeah, of course.

270
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,880
